{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas","id":1543944,"title":"VTR 2E - Unaligned player story hook ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-15T20:45:39-07:00","id":1543944,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> VTR 2E - Unaligned player story hook ideas?","content":"I have an unaligned Ventrue: Macellarius bloodline player that has very little contact with other kindred for fear of getting caught up in vampire games and his only real friends are an Ivory Claw that newly became an alpha along with a Gangral is recently met at Elysium, that helped him survive an attack by The Brood on his haven. The player lost his ghoul/haven in a fire and diablerized one of The Brood in secret by the end of the scene. The player mostly interacts with female Mortal\u2019s, eats weird food, sometimes pokes his nose in Uratha business and I wanna maintain the Requiem feel in the chronicle. Thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T01:38:46-07:00","id":1543959,"title":"","content":"Nothing too fancy on my part, just some questions to cover the basics:<br /> <br /> - Why did The Brood attack the PC, in his haven to boot, in the first place? Their knowing it's location implies either the PC got sloppy or they had been stalking him for some time, what raises questions.<br /> <br /> - One of the Brood attackers was diablerized, but what about the others, anyone else met final death or did they all escape? How many attackers there were, for that matter? Could any survivors have feelings over the matter and want payback, consider the PC's success a sign of potential as a new convert or any sort of other weird ideas<br /> <br /> - Did the PC see his ghoul die in the fire or could something happen to its body, like receiving compulsory embrace and conversion into The Brood or spontaneously rising as a Revenant or Larva a few nights later? If the ghoul is truly dead and gone, could the circunstances behind its death not lead to its return as a ghost haunting the fire's location or something else depending on the dead person's circunstances?<br /> <br /> - Where does the PC rest during the daylight hours now that his haven went into the flames? How (im)permanent is that new set-up supposed to be? Is he crashing at the place of one of his usual mortal victims or something else? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> - Could there be other Brood members in the area beside those who attacked the PC? Would they be allies or rivals of that first group?<br /> <br /> - What other kindred - recognized or off-the-grid - exist in the PC's area or neighboring city districts? How (un)important are they in the city's nightlife? Could any of those locals move in to &quot;take over&quot; the PC's old turf now that he has been borderline expelled from it? Would any of them <b>want </b>to, considering the place seems to have been targeted already? Would any of them even know it was a Brood pack/coven in the first place? Could any of those &quot;undead neighbors&quot; have been the targets of similar attacks, by the same or other groups?<br /> <br /> - The PC diablerized a Brood member, now what? Did he increase in Blood Potency or not, gained a skill or discipline dot or something else? What kind of hooks could you come up with from sudden memory flashes of the consumed kindred's perspective? Could those lingering memories and impulses produce unexpected effects like forming a new anchor, bane, etc, among other possibilities, muddling one's sense of identity?<br /> <br /> - The Gangrel that helped the PC, what can you tell us about him (or her) - is it Unaligned too or beholden to one of the Covenants, does it beling to some bloodline, how well-connected or not is it, at least compared to the PC? Since the two of them met each other at Elysium, it's my understanding the PC <i>already </i>belongs to the local court, even if in a minor and distant role, so there's potential for some waves there, either from some kindred already knowing about the attack or either of the two of them calling attention to it.<br /> <br /> - As an aside, how did the PC become a Macellarius in the first place, where is his sire or Avus?<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully, answering some or all of those should help you to come up with at least a few hooks to fill out the PC's future misadventures.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T02:47:15-07:00","id":1543961,"title":"","content":"While he can try getting away without trying to get caught up in vampire games, there's no real way to not get caught up in vampire society. <br /> <br /> Where does your character live and hunt? Why does he have rights to feeding grounds there? If given/granted/approved by some vampire authority, why is that authority not expecting him to _contribute_ to the city and the order there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T03:15:13-07:00","id":1543968,"title":"","content":"It would be helpful to figure out what you think <i>Vampire - the Requiem</i> is about. For the purpose of this post, I'll assume its major aspects are:<br /> \u2022 Political and interpersonal scheming<br /> \u2022 Struggle for survival and power<br /> \u2022 Searching for meaning in unlife<br /> \u2022 Moral compromises<br /> and finally \u2022 Difficult choices between those four<br /> <br /> Covenants usually inform how those scenarios play out. Do you struggle with/against political players of Invictus, or bizarre academics of Ordo Dracul? Do you find power in Blood Sorcery or networking of Carthians? Note that staying Unaligned does not remove those factors. Your character still wants to survive and ensure their independence and the world won't give those up easily. He has to deal with the Brood, Covenants, Prince's Court, minor and major power players - all of which have an angle and see him as an asset or an obstacle, and all of which can be played against one another.<br /> <br /> Notice how your major ally is in a position of prominence among Uratha, and is also a member of Ivory Claws - a Tribe that schemes and networks on par with Vampires. You can essentially see your Macellarius as a low-ranking member of the Pure. This would be a fitting tragedy for Requiem - a character runs away from power games of Vampires, not only to fail, but also to ensnare themselves in power games of Werewolves. They now have to justify their existence to other Ivory Claws, so the Alpha does not lose credibility for their friendship, protect them from the Forsaken and competitors, justify themselves to Kindred authorities for consorting with dangerous outsiders, all the while surviving interaction with Raging killing machines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T04:26:16-07:00","id":1543972,"title":"","content":"Once some random mekhet sees you, and learns that you're a diablerist, why wouldn't they be reporting you to authorities? You have nothing to offer. Why would the said authorities not decide that you should be executed? Why would they allow a random diablerist, with no real ties (read Value) to the society around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T07:03:14-07:00","id":1543981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas#post1543944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an unaligned Ventrue: Macellarius bloodline player that has very little contact with other kindred for fear of getting caught up in vampire games and his only real friends are an Ivory Claw that newly became an alpha along with a Gangral is recently met at Elysium, that helped him survive an attack by The Brood on his haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, what is the story behind the player being a lone Macellarius with no ties within the city's undead society? Gluttons as a bloodline tend to be well-connected, to each other if nobody else at least, for the sake of pooling resources in the maintenance of extended herds according to their peculiar proclivities Has him already delved in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gustus\" target=\"_blank\">Gustus</a>, bloodline banes and all the baggage that comes with it?<br /> <br /> Maybe i'm just shooting at random things in the dark, but it <b><i>did </i></b>cross my mind in passing the idea of the Brood being interested in the PC for something related to either his sire or another kindred ancestor from the bloodline. The discipline would not be out of place as a tool among the Forsworn ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-16-2024, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T07:03:52-07:00","id":1543982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas?p=1543972#post1543972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once some random mekhet sees you, and learns that you're a diablerist, why wouldn't they be reporting you to authorities? You have nothing to offer. Why would the said authorities not decide that you should be executed? Why would they allow a random diablerist, with no real ties (read Value) to the society around?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games - at least in settled up domains, secrets sniffed out through Auspex are hardly used as definitive proof of guiltness. The Prince may also believe the random Meketh, or being able to use Auspex himself, but in front of his court, you need solid proofs. Otherwise the risk is that the prince could condemn whoever he like, saying that through Auspex he discovered his secret.<br /> <br /> That being said, behind the curtain, they can still act as per their acquired knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-16-2024, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T09:45:48-07:00","id":1543994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas?p=1543982#post1543982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my games - at least in settled up domains, secrets sniffed out through Auspex are hardly used as definitive proof of guiltness. The Prince may also believe the random Meketh, or being able to use Auspex himself, but in front of his court, you need solid proofs. Otherwise the risk is that the prince could condemn whoever he like, saying that through Auspex he discovered his secret.<br /> <br /> That being said, behind the curtain, they can still act as per their acquired knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure, however, we're not talking about a member of our society. We're talking about someone who's avoiding contact, is avoiding getting indebted, and involved in it's workings.<br /> <br /> Also on your risk - how risky is it? especially if the said person is brought upon the court, and any Auspex user could inspect them. If the prince was fabricating shit, then he'd have to be powerful enough for _all_ auspex users to stay quiet, both inpeson in court, but also in private whispers.<br /> <br /> This case however? Nobody has a reason to stand up for this person, everyone has a reason to fear him (diablerist, after all). And while burden of proof would be required, and wanted to maintain peace at court, we potentially have none of that here.<br /> <br /> Even without real diablerie here, which will show up to auspex, some flimsy evidence of &quot;wrong&quot; doing, would potentially be sufficient for the public eye to be &quot;yup, prince is taking care of the city by eliminating this person.&quot;. In this case, we have real diablerie marks upon this characters soul.<br /> <br /> This is a no-brainer for the Prince. With a little bit of skill (and surely, Prince has plenty of skill and relationships with the harpies, right?) this can be twisted into a win story for the Prince, and for whomever brought this info to them.<br /> <br /> Something a lot of characters who are afraid of to be indebted often forget is that being in debt - can be a good thing. Whoever you owe, is interested in your wellbeing, the better off you are, the easier, and the bigger, pay out they can expect to be able to cash out later. <br /> <br /> With no leverage over this character, (or relationship), nobody has any real interest in protecting him either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 10-16-2024, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T12:27:04-07:00","id":1544009,"title":"","content":"To give a bit more background, the players Sire is currently being blood hunted due to theft of a potent book of lore that was in the Prince\u2019s possession, and a supposed betrayal of two covenants (Crone &amp; Ordo Dracul). The Brood attacked because the player and his Ivory Claw friend (another PC) learned way too much about their nefarious dealings with some dark wolves at a Wound site via a troubled mortal (and his 3 friends) the players got wrapped up with. The Kindred players abandoned ghoul clung to life long enough to drink from a torpor Brood at the attack site and now she\u2019s begun her vengeful Requiem. As far as leftover Brood, the Sun caught them before they could get to safety as they had to attempt to avoid encountering the other players nearby pack. Police and the Fire Dept are involved now and the Kindred is hold-up in a motel in Venice, California 30 mins from the burned down attack site (his haven). The Brood attack was loud, strange things occurred and there were mortal witnesses to parts of the attack. Now\u2026it\u2019s on the Princes radar\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11532-dpowell","name":"DPowell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11532_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T13:05:25-07:00","id":1544017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas?p=1544009#post1544009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give a bit more background, the players Sire is currently being blood hunted due to theft of a potent book of lore that was in the Prince\u2019s possession, and a supposed betrayal of two covenants (Crone &amp; Ordo Dracul).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, just wow. This guy could be a major character in the Malazan Books of the Fallen based on just sheer bridgeburning skills. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> PC must be very lucky indeed the Prince didn't blood bond him as possible accomplice or some equally cheap &amp; flimsy excuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas?p=1544009#post1544009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Brood attacked because the player and his Ivory Claw friend (another PC) learned way too much about their nefarious dealings with some dark wolves at a Wound site via a troubled mortal (and his 3 friends) the players got wrapped up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know it's a mixed group, i was already half suspecting so based on comments on the Ivory Claw but confirmation is good.<br /> Dark Wolves? Honestly not familiar. Could be related to one of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Uratha#Other_Groups\" target=\"_blank\">those</a>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas?p=1544009#post1544009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kindred players abandoned ghoul clung to life long enough to drink from a torpor Brood at the attack site and now she\u2019s begun her vengeful Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basic and classic. Incidentally, blood sympathy or weird Brood rituals could led to who knows what kind of weirdness with this ex-ghoul turned vengeful neonate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DPowell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas?p=1544009#post1544009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as leftover Brood, the Sun caught them before they could get to safety as they had to attempt to avoid encountering the other players nearby pack. Police and the Fire Dept are involved now and the Kindred is hold-up in a motel in Venice, California 30 mins from the burned down attack site (his haven). The Brood attack was loud, strange things occurred and there were mortal witnesses to parts of the attack. Now\u2026it\u2019s on the Princes radar\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Things really <b>not </b>looking good for the Macellarius - either he starts looking for some way to molify the Prince and spare his lousy hide or he better make plans for either moving out or some decades in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-16-2024, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T15:12:47-07:00","id":1544025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1543944-vtr-2e-unaligned-player-story-hook-ideas?p=1544017#post1544017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue ani